<figure class="pipeline-overview" aria-label="Example: convert Markdown files to HTML">
  <figcaption>Example: convert Markdown files to HTML</figcaption>
  <ol class="pipeline-steps">
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/programming_guide/app/">App</a>
      <p>Starts the pipeline with the source and output directories.</p>
      <span class="relationship">Runs processing components <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h16m-6-6 6 6-6 6" /></svg></span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/programming_guide/processing_component/">Processing component</a>
      <p>Processes a source file. Calls <a href="/docs/programming_guide/function/">functions</a> to read Markdown and produce HTML.</p>
      <span class="relationship">Declares target states <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h16m-6-6 6 6-6 6" /></svg></span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/docs/programming_guide/target_state/">Target state</a>
      <p>Describes the output file: its name and HTML content.</p>
      <span class="relationship">CocoIndex updates the output</span>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p class="pipeline-result">When the component finishes, CocoIndex creates, updates, or removes its output files as needed.</p>
</figure>

